        "class": "view-mode-section view-mode-section__branch view-mode-section__branch--human"
      },
      "html": "<div class=\"w-full bg-chalk\"><section class=\"blog-reading-shell pointer-events-auto\" data-v-1c6297c3><nav class=\"blog-breadcrumb\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/feed\">Blogs</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span>Google Ads</span></nav><article aria-labelledby=\"blog-30-title\"><header class=\"blog-article-header\"><p class=\"blog-eyebrow\">Paid Media &amp; Content</p><h1 id=\"blog-30-title\">How to review a Google Ads management proposal</h1><p class=\"blog-article-summary\">Review a Google Ads proposal for audience intent, conversion definitions, account ownership and the work needed after the click.</p><p class=\"blog-byline\">Fyntix Editorial · Updated <time datetime=\"2026-11-24\">24 Nov 2026</time> · 2 min read</p></header><nav class=\"blog-contents\" aria-label=\"On this page\"><p>On this page</p><ol><li><a href=\"#blog-30-section-1\">Clarify the audience and campaign purpose</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-30-section-2\">Ask what counts as a conversion</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-30-section-3\">Include the destination and the message</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-30-section-4\">Review access, reporting and change control</a></li></ol></nav><div class=\"blog-prose\"><p>A Google Ads proposal should explain how campaign management will support the business's offer and sales process. A list of account tasks is useful, but it does not establish whether the team understands the customer response you need.</p>\n<p>Use the proposal to review the whole path from a search to an enquiry or purchase. Ask who owns each part, what information is required and how the agency will decide whether the work is helping.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-30-section-1\">Clarify the audience and campaign purpose</h2>\n<p>The proposal should identify the service, market and search intent it plans to investigate. Ask how the team will distinguish relevant demand from loosely related searches. Check whether brand, new-customer discovery and other purposes are being discussed clearly.</p>\n<p>For an illustrative specialist service, broad industry interest may be less useful than a narrower group of people looking for a specific solution. The account structure should reflect the business decision rather than simply reproduce a keyword list.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-30-section-2\">Ask what counts as a conversion</h2>\n<p>Confirm whether the programme measures submissions, calls, bookings, purchases or another defined action. Ask how those events will be checked and how sales feedback can inform the review. A form total alone may not show whether the campaign attracts suitable customers.</p>\n<p>Google Ads distinguishes qualified leads and converted leads in its conversion-goal guidance. Where appropriate, discuss the information and process needed to connect later lead stages with the campaign. The business needs a workable feedback route for that information to remain useful.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-30-section-3\">Include the destination and the message</h2>\n<p>Ask who reviews landing-page content, form usability and the relationship between the advertisement and the page. Clarify whether proposed improvements are included, separately scoped or expected from your internal team.</p>\n<p>The campaign can expose questions the page does not answer. A useful management arrangement gives those observations a route into content and website improvements rather than limiting the discussion to account settings.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-30-section-4\">Review access, reporting and change control</h2>\n<p>Confirm account ownership, the working team's access and the handover process. Ask for a sample report showing spending, useful responses and next actions. Understand which changes can happen within the agreed plan and which require approval.</p>\n<p>Fyntix's Google Ads service connects intent, campaigns, creative and conversion reporting. A good proposal should make that connection understandable and identify the responsibilities needed on both sides. You can read Google's own explanation of <a href=\"https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/11459091?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">qualified and converted leads</a> when preparing the measurement discussion.</p></div><aside class=\"blog-service-callout\" aria-label=\"Work with Fyntix\"><p class=\"blog-eyebrow\">Put the idea into practice</p><h2>Plan your next step with Fyntix.</h2><p>Connect your audience and offer with a practical plan for search visibility, paid media and useful content.</p><div class=\"blog-callout-links\"><a href=\"/contact\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full\">Book a free strategy call</a><a href=\"/services#service-google-ads\">Explore the relevant service</a></div></aside></article></section></div>"
